nothing-to-test = Nothing is bound to the device in use, so there is no chain to test. Shape a curve under Bands first.
not-levellable = The chain cannot be level-matched to its bypass, so it is not tested
not-playing = Play a song first: the test is heard on one playing, and a DSD stream sent as it is cannot be switched within
alike = A and B would sound the same on this stream, so there is nothing to tell apart
not-measured = A and B could not be measured against each other, so the test cannot level them
too-far-apart = A and B play too far apart in loudness to be matched, so the test cannot level them
trials-refused = The listening test takes between one and a hundred trials
measuring = Measuring…
starting = Starting…
-how-it-works = X is one of the two, drawn afresh for every trial: hear A, B and X as often as you like on the song playing, then say which X was. A change is heard a few moments after you press, within the audio already buffered.
a-is-the-equaliser-as-set = A is the equaliser as set, B is the signal with it bypassed. Each is lowered, never raised, until their loudness across 20 Hz to 16 kHz agrees to 0.1 dB, so the louder one cannot give itself away. The room correction stays on in both. { -how-it-works }
a-is-lossy-restoration-as-set = A is lossy restoration as set, B the setting you choose. Restoration changes how loud a song plays, so the song is first measured through both, which takes a moment, and the louder is lowered, never raised, until the two agree. A lossless file is touched by neither. { -how-it-works }
a-is-the-resampler-as-set = A is the resampler as set, B the quality and phase you choose. Both play at one level. The resampler works only where the song's rate has to be changed to the device's; where it does not, the two sound alike and the test is refused. { -how-it-works }
a-is-the-dither-as-set = A is the dither as set, B the kind and shaping you choose. Both play at one level. Dither works only where the bits are cut down to the device's depth; where they are not, the two sound alike and the test is refused. { -how-it-works }
